WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:06.272
-Well rested and ready to go.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:08.775
It's so good to see everybody.
I am in a good mood.

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:12.579
Last Saturday was
the Creative Arts Emmys

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:14.580
in Los Angeles, California,

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.517
where "Corrections"
was nominated.

00:00:19.485 --> 00:00:21.821
You guys want to see an Emmy?

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:23.156
Do you?

00:00:24.123 --> 00:00:25.291
Me too.

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:27.093
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.495 --> 00:00:31.664
Me too.

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:35.935
Can give you the name of
a couple of late night hosts

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:37.937
who have plenty at their house.

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:39.606
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.408 --> 00:00:45.445
Me and Shoemaker went, and...

00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:52.051
Suffice it to say,
Mikey the Shoe don't like L.A.

00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:54.520
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.855
He lands in a bad mood.

00:00:56.855 --> 00:01:00.693
Complains the whole time.

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:03.028
Says stuff like,

00:01:03.028 --> 00:01:04.564
"If I wanted green juice,

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:07.233
I'll drink it from
a jar of Claussens."

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:09.402
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:13.406
So, it's like...

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:15.875
It starts bad
and it just gets worse

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:17.543
because we...

00:01:17.543 --> 00:01:18.978
Donna from Wardrobe...

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:20.813
We decided sort of
last minute to go,

00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:23.616
and we were off all month,
and our tuxes were here.

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:26.519
And so we wrote
Donna from Wardrobe,

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:29.321
who very kindly
put together a box,

00:01:29.321 --> 00:01:32.492
a garment box,
and sent it to us at our hotel.

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:34.927
So anyway, I'm getting ready
for the Emmys,

00:01:34.927 --> 00:01:37.730
and Mikey the Shoe calls up
and he goes,

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:41.567
"I think she sent
two of your shirts."

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:44.069
And he goes...
How'd you say it?

00:01:44.069 --> 00:01:46.139
"Mine don't fit so good"?

00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:49.142
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:52.612
So he comes up to my room,
and I'm like...

00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:53.946
Based on the fit,

00:01:53.946 --> 00:01:55.348
I don't think it was
one of my shirts.

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:58.051
It was maybe
one of Frisbee's shirts.

00:01:58.051 --> 00:01:59.685
It was not even close,
and he's going like,

00:01:59.685 --> 00:02:01.320
"Maybe I'll wear it backwards
like a smock."

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:03.156
I'm like, "What?"

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:05.491
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.491 --> 00:02:08.060
So he goes, "I got one."

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:12.231
"Don't worry, I got one
in my room, but it's blue."

00:02:12.231 --> 00:02:15.201
So, we go to the Emmys

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:17.236
and Mikey the Shoe
is in a tuxedo

00:02:17.236 --> 00:02:19.405
with just a blue shirt,

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:22.408
which he keeps saying
is "Bronx formal."

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:25.311
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:27.914
"If it's good enough
for Danny Aiello..."

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:29.315
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:32.985
Anyway.

00:02:32.985 --> 00:02:36.522
Look, I know they voted ahead
of time and it had been decided

00:02:36.522 --> 00:02:38.624
that we had not won
when we showed up.

00:02:38.624 --> 00:02:40.693
But I think if they'd seen
Mikey the Shoe

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:42.829
and his blue shirt,
if we were the winner,

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:44.998
they would have just
crossed it off.

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:47.500
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.135
Eminem was a big winner
that night.

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:50.970
The Super Bowl halftime show,
deservedly --

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:53.172
was fantastic --
won an Emmy.

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:56.642
And we mentioned that
in a monologue this week

00:02:56.642 --> 00:02:59.945
that with the Emmy
that Eminem won,

00:02:59.945 --> 00:03:02.949
he now only needs a Tony
for the EGOT.

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:05.651
We joked that you should keep
an eye out for him

00:03:05.651 --> 00:03:07.420
in "Dear Evan Hansen."

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:10.589
Now, more than one
Broadway aficionado amongst you

00:03:10.589 --> 00:03:14.593
pointed out that show
is no longer Tony-eligible.

00:03:14.593 --> 00:03:17.396
So, in order for Eminem
to win a Tony for that show,

00:03:17.396 --> 00:03:19.899
he would either have to be
in a revival

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:22.735
or -- bear with me --
a new show called

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:26.739
"Dear Evan, Stan's Son."

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:29.242
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:30.776
Here's the idea.

00:03:30.776 --> 00:03:34.714
It's an alternate take
on the Stan saga where Stan dies

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:37.417
but his girlfriend lives
and then has the baby.

00:03:37.417 --> 00:03:40.620
And she names the baby Evan.
And it's a story about Eminem

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.922
befriending young Evan
because he feels bad

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:45.091
that he never wrote back
his now-dead dad.

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:48.127
I don't have time
to write this.

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:49.729
That's an idea
for whoever wants it.

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:54.066
I am so behind the eight ball
in "Cicada, Cicada" right now.

00:03:54.066 --> 00:03:57.569
It's going way too slowly,
and I'm racing against the clock

00:03:57.569 --> 00:04:00.739
because if the Mets win
the World Series this year,

00:04:00.739 --> 00:04:04.243
I'm [bleep] 'cause
that is my whole third act.

00:04:04.243 --> 00:04:06.645
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.645 --> 00:04:08.848
And if you're surprised
that it's a three-act play,

00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:10.750
it's actually four.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.251
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.251 --> 00:04:15.788
But the fourth act
is just a Q&amp;A.

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:18.625
With pre-vetted questions.

00:04:21.294 --> 00:04:25.130
We also mentioned a news story
about images of the Titanic.

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:26.999
The highest resolution
photos ever

00:04:26.999 --> 00:04:29.469
were taken
of the Titanic wreckage.

00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:31.804
And we said,
but now the bad news --

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:33.172
no survivors.

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:36.008
And you guys, a bunch you said

00:04:36.008 --> 00:04:39.011
there were, of course,
survivors from the Titanic.

00:04:39.011 --> 00:04:40.012
We knew that.

00:04:40.012 --> 00:04:41.547
Our joke was based on the fact

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:45.818
that you'd go down there now
and find a survivor.

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:47.686
Which brings up an interesting
ethical question.

00:04:47.686 --> 00:04:50.690
If you did find one,

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:54.027
let's say a 110-year-old person
who somehow, I don't know,

00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:58.631
there's an air pocket
in the... galley?

00:04:58.631 --> 00:05:00.032
Boat kitchen.

00:05:00.032 --> 00:05:04.670
And, or maybe the saltwater
has helped preserve them,

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:06.605
but they're, you know,
a robust, happy,

00:05:06.605 --> 00:05:08.941
I don't know,
110-year-old person.

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:11.777
Do you bring them up?

00:05:11.777 --> 00:05:14.280
Or at this point,
would it just be too jarring?

00:05:16.415 --> 00:05:17.884
I don't know.

00:05:19.618 --> 00:05:21.787
Speaking of the ocean...

00:05:21.787 --> 00:05:23.890
Oh, son of a gun, I...

00:05:25.991 --> 00:05:27.627
We'll save that one.

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:30.196
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.196 --> 00:05:32.698
Shoemaker, next week
during "Corrections,"

00:05:32.698 --> 00:05:35.034
just yell out
"speaking of the ocean."

00:05:35.034 --> 00:05:37.703
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.703 --> 00:05:41.340
I quoted a Bob Dylan lyric
in our last "Corrections"

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:44.476
as his famous song,
"It's Not Me, Lady."

00:05:44.476 --> 00:05:45.811
A bunch of you,

00:05:45.811 --> 00:05:47.646
the ones who recognize jokes
the best,

00:05:47.646 --> 00:05:50.049
said the line is actually,
"It ain't me, babe."

00:05:52.885 --> 00:05:54.720
[ Under breath ]
Come away from my window...

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:57.723
Leave at your own chosen speed,
I'm not the one you want, babe,

00:05:57.723 --> 00:05:59.725
I'm not the one you need...

00:05:59.725 --> 00:06:01.093
You say you're looking
for someone

00:06:01.093 --> 00:06:02.762
who's never weak
and always strong,

00:06:02.762 --> 00:06:05.664
support you and protect you
whether you're right or wrong,

00:06:05.664 --> 00:06:07.599
someone to open each
and every door...

00:06:07.599 --> 00:06:09.635
[ Louder] It's not me, lady.
No, I was right.

00:06:12.705 --> 00:06:17.009
That, of course, is a great song
off the classic album

00:06:17.009 --> 00:06:19.445
"Bob Dylan,
But This Time From the Left."

00:06:19.445 --> 00:06:21.079
[ Laughter ]

00:06:22.114 --> 00:06:24.082
I said Rudy married
his second cousin,

00:06:24.082 --> 00:06:26.852
but then I referenced the
daughter of his first cousin.

00:06:26.852 --> 00:06:29.588
The daughter of his first cousin
would be his first cousin

00:06:29.588 --> 00:06:30.923
once removed.

00:06:30.923 --> 00:06:33.158
A lot of you were very,

00:06:33.158 --> 00:06:35.293
very passionate
about that correction in a way

00:06:35.293 --> 00:06:38.431
that makes me think it's
something you've angrily yelled

00:06:38.431 --> 00:06:40.733
at a skeptical
justice of the peace.

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:42.067
[ Laughter ]

00:06:42.067 --> 00:06:45.238
"I'm not saying it's right!
I'm saying it's legal!"

00:06:45.238 --> 00:06:46.839
[ Laughter ]

00:06:49.175 --> 00:06:51.710
Second cousins is when
your parents are first cousins.

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:53.179
Second cousin once removed

00:06:53.179 --> 00:06:56.215
is when you marry your second
cousin and then divorce them.

00:06:56.215 --> 00:06:58.384
[ Laughter ]

00:06:58.384 --> 00:07:00.052
You guys, we make a lot of fun
of Rudy

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:02.988
for the old cousin mix-up.

00:07:02.988 --> 00:07:05.691
But you know who married
his first cousin?

00:07:05.691 --> 00:07:07.693
Albert Einstein.

00:07:07.693 --> 00:07:11.029
Albert Einstein.
This was courtesy of you guys.

00:07:11.029 --> 00:07:15.134
Albert Einstein's second wife
was his first cousin.

00:07:15.134 --> 00:07:18.304
Their mothers were sisters
and their fathers were cousins,

00:07:18.304 --> 00:07:21.674
which means they were both first
and second cousins.

00:07:23.942 --> 00:07:25.110
They never had kids.

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:27.113
Thank God!

00:07:27.113 --> 00:07:30.783
[ Laughter ]

00:07:30.783 --> 00:07:32.151
Don't need to be a physicist
to know

00:07:32.151 --> 00:07:34.453
that would have been a bad idea.

00:07:34.453 --> 00:07:37.489
We had a month off, a little bit
too much time to have off.

00:07:37.489 --> 00:07:39.358
I got to be honest, very happy
to be back this week.

00:07:39.358 --> 00:07:40.959
I think we're all very happy.

00:07:40.959 --> 00:07:44.396
It was nice
to catch up on stuff.

00:07:44.396 --> 00:07:45.998
Shows, movies, books.

00:07:45.998 --> 00:07:47.299
There was that, um,

00:07:47.299 --> 00:07:49.435
"The Lord of the Rings:
The Rings of Power."

00:07:49.435 --> 00:07:52.271
Super succinct title.
Classic Tolkien style.

00:07:52.271 --> 00:07:53.939
[ Laughter ]

00:07:53.939 --> 00:07:56.943
"The Lord of the Rings:
The Rings of Power."

00:07:59.045 --> 00:08:01.046
I haven't seen it.
I guess it's on Amazon,

00:08:01.046 --> 00:08:04.216
but I couldn't watch it,
because I'm a 48-year-old man.

00:08:04.216 --> 00:08:06.085
[ Laughter ]

00:08:13.226 --> 00:08:14.560
Mugs!

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:16.729
So, last time we were here,

00:08:16.729 --> 00:08:18.364
I said, the mugs were
available online.

00:08:18.364 --> 00:08:21.567
And guys, you backed me up.

00:08:21.567 --> 00:08:23.402
The mugs were a hit.

00:08:23.402 --> 00:08:25.070
The mugs, on the first day,
sold out,

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:28.039
I think both due
to your enthusiasm

00:08:28.039 --> 00:08:31.577
and maybe the doubtful nature
of those in the NBC Store

00:08:31.577 --> 00:08:35.314
who ordered
the first set of mugs.

00:08:35.314 --> 00:08:38.283
But this is true. It really did.
All jokes aside, it went great.

00:08:38.283 --> 00:08:39.718
These are...It was...

00:08:39.718 --> 00:08:48.227
It is the best-selling mug
on the NBC.com store ever.

00:08:48.227 --> 00:08:52.231
That's just a...
That's a true thing.

00:08:52.231 --> 00:08:55.001
The worst-selling is, uh...

00:08:56.401 --> 00:08:57.903
...Chicago Mug.

00:08:57.903 --> 00:08:59.906
[ Laughter ]

00:09:05.978 --> 00:09:09.749
And I guess they don't even sell
the "To Catch a Predator" mug.

00:09:09.749 --> 00:09:12.517
[ Laughter ]

00:09:12.517 --> 00:09:14.353
Yeah, it's kind of...
This part, I like.

00:09:14.353 --> 00:09:16.856
It says, "Why don't you have
a seat over there?"

00:09:16.856 --> 00:09:18.624
[ Laughter ]

00:09:21.293 --> 00:09:22.794
And this...
But I'm worried because I guess

00:09:22.794 --> 00:09:25.164
this one's available soon,
with Keith Morrison

00:09:25.164 --> 00:09:27.199
drinking a mug with a picture
of Keith Morrison

00:09:27.199 --> 00:09:28.868
drinking a mug.

00:09:28.868 --> 00:09:31.137
[ Laughter ]

00:09:33.205 --> 00:09:34.373
Guys...

00:09:34.373 --> 00:09:36.375
These are are the data
on the mugs.

00:09:36.375 --> 00:09:41.313
We're really excited.
It's sold 1,369 units.

00:09:41.313 --> 00:09:43.649
Now, you might be thinking
"Oh, is a unit just one mug?"

00:09:43.649 --> 00:09:44.716
You're right. Yes.

00:09:44.716 --> 00:09:47.886
So, that's 1,369 mugs.

00:09:47.886 --> 00:09:50.389
But that does not count
the physical store.

00:09:50.389 --> 00:09:52.424
The physical store has sold 59,

00:09:52.424 --> 00:09:53.625
so I should have
put that one first.

00:09:53.625 --> 00:09:55.161
That's not a big number.

00:09:55.161 --> 00:09:56.529
[ Laughter ]

00:09:56.529 --> 00:09:58.531
Only 17 complaints
about the mug.

00:09:58.531 --> 00:10:01.900
Some of you have posted photos
on Twitter of a --

00:10:01.900 --> 00:10:03.535
Very kind of you.

00:10:03.535 --> 00:10:05.538
You've opened up your mugs
and they're just shattered.

00:10:05.538 --> 00:10:07.472
It does seem like
they're in a million pieces.

00:10:07.472 --> 00:10:09.641
I don't know.
I don't know how that happened.

00:10:09.641 --> 00:10:12.144
I do, we do want
to replace those mugs.

00:10:12.144 --> 00:10:14.012
So just, if you could just send
a photo of that,

00:10:14.012 --> 00:10:15.647
we do obviously need to know
it's you, so just send

00:10:15.647 --> 00:10:17.116
a photo of that mug

00:10:17.116 --> 00:10:19.284
with your driver's license
and your Social Security number

00:10:19.284 --> 00:10:20.286
and, uh...

00:10:20.286 --> 00:10:21.954
[ Laughter ]

00:10:24.323 --> 00:10:27.459
Some of us asked are the mugs
dishwasher and microwave safe.

00:10:27.459 --> 00:10:28.794
They are.
Thank you for asking.

00:10:28.794 --> 00:10:31.063
We did a lot of testing
to make sure.

00:10:31.063 --> 00:10:32.898
That was the --
that was the hold-up.

00:10:32.898 --> 00:10:35.234
That's why it took a year,
is we wanted to make sure.

00:10:35.234 --> 00:10:37.069
The whole, the first,
the beta test,

00:10:37.069 --> 00:10:39.372
a lot of them were either dish--
they were one or the other,

00:10:39.372 --> 00:10:40.806
and you could wash it
in the dishwasher

00:10:40.806 --> 00:10:41.807
and everything was fine,

00:10:41.807 --> 00:10:43.809
but if you put it
in the microwave,

00:10:43.809 --> 00:10:45.344
just loss of life.

00:10:45.344 --> 00:10:49.047
So we lost some good people,
a lot of good people,

00:10:49.047 --> 00:10:52.718
but you can put it wherever
you want,

00:10:52.718 --> 00:10:56.055
except a box
surrounded by bubble wrap.

00:10:56.055 --> 00:10:58.790
[ Laughter ]

00:10:58.790 --> 00:11:02.995
Oh, so, I mentioned
the Emmys, and...

00:11:04.029 --> 00:11:05.431
I...

00:11:06.832 --> 00:11:09.668
Look, we didn't win, but had we,
I did take it seriously.

00:11:09.668 --> 00:11:12.438
I never want to be one of those
people who you win an award

00:11:12.438 --> 00:11:14.040
and doesn't know
what he's going to say.

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:21.446
And I had some things to say
about the jackal in my speech.

00:11:21.446 --> 00:11:25.884
And I mentioned that to one
of our writers, Seth Reiss,

00:11:25.884 --> 00:11:27.686
who said, "You should read
that speech

00:11:27.686 --> 00:11:29.688
in the next 'Corrections.'"

00:11:29.688 --> 00:11:33.526
Which is funny because
that's what I was going to do,

00:11:33.526 --> 00:11:36.028
and now I can't!

00:11:36.028 --> 00:11:37.195
[ Laughter ]

00:11:37.195 --> 00:11:40.866
Because now if I do,
it's also his idea.

00:11:40.866 --> 00:11:43.201
[ Laughter ]

00:11:43.201 --> 00:11:44.703
And next time I see him,
he'll be like,

00:11:44.703 --> 00:11:47.372
"Ehh? Pretty good!"

00:11:47.372 --> 00:11:49.542
This isn't for you.

00:11:49.542 --> 00:11:51.043
[ Laughter ]

00:11:51.043 --> 00:11:56.115
Get your hands off it.
This is mine.

00:11:56.115 --> 00:11:58.317
You don't see me
trying to jump on to...

00:12:00.619 --> 00:12:01.954
What has he...?

00:12:01.954 --> 00:12:03.422
[ Laughter ]

00:12:06.425 --> 00:12:08.260
"Actathlon"?

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:09.594
[ Laughter ]

00:12:09.594 --> 00:12:12.498
2017's "Actathlon"?

00:12:17.970 --> 00:12:19.838
Now, in Reiss' defense,

00:12:19.838 --> 00:12:21.606
I want to be sincere
for a moment.

00:12:21.606 --> 00:12:23.275
He has been very busy.

00:12:23.275 --> 00:12:26.812
He wrote a major motion picture.

00:12:26.812 --> 00:12:28.279
It's got a trailer
and everything.

00:12:28.279 --> 00:12:30.749
The trailer looks fantastic.
It's called "The Menu."

00:12:30.749 --> 00:12:33.251
Ralph Fiennes, Anya Taylor-Joy,
Nicholas Hoult,

00:12:33.251 --> 00:12:34.586
Hong Chau, Janet McTeer.

00:12:34.586 --> 00:12:35.620
Trailer's fantastic.

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:37.723
It is premiering
this weekend at TIFF,

00:12:37.723 --> 00:12:41.494
the Toronto International
Film Festival.

00:12:41.494 --> 00:12:45.998
And we are so genuinely
so proud of him.

00:12:45.998 --> 00:12:49.935
He's a great writer,
and it never stops being cool

00:12:49.935 --> 00:12:53.339
when people who work here go on
and succeed somewhere else.

00:12:53.339 --> 00:12:56.508
I should note, he co-wrote it
with Will Tracy,

00:12:56.508 --> 00:12:58.343
who I haven't met,

00:12:58.343 --> 00:13:01.146
but who I assume
has the patience of Job.

00:13:01.146 --> 00:13:03.115
[ Laughter ]

00:13:07.353 --> 00:13:10.189
Will writes for "Succession"
and used to write

00:13:10.189 --> 00:13:13.859
for "Last Week Tonight,"
so head on over to his place

00:13:13.859 --> 00:13:15.861
if you want to see
one of those Emmys.

00:13:15.861 --> 00:13:17.663
[ Laughter ]

00:13:20.399 --> 00:13:22.901
Reiss is very excited
and he said...

00:13:22.901 --> 00:13:25.337
It's cool. He left.
He went down. He was on set.

00:13:25.337 --> 00:13:28.607
He said he got to be really
good friends with the cast.

00:13:28.607 --> 00:13:30.175
Although I have my doubts,

00:13:30.175 --> 00:13:32.845
'cause he keeps saying
"Ralph" "Fee-en-ness."

00:13:32.845 --> 00:13:34.013
[ Laughter ]

00:13:38.050 --> 00:13:40.051
So in the end, Reiss did give me
an idea for "Corrections,"

00:13:40.051 --> 00:13:43.088
just wasn't the one he wanted.
[ Laughs ]

00:13:43.088 --> 00:13:45.590
But here's to the premiere,

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:47.426
the TIFF premiere
of "The Menu."

00:13:47.426 --> 00:13:48.827
We're so excited to see it.

00:13:48.827 --> 00:13:53.498
Here's to being back
with everyone who watches this.

00:13:53.498 --> 00:13:56.067
Cheers to everyone
who's got their jackal mug.

00:13:56.067 --> 00:13:59.204
And let's have
a wonderful fall together.

00:13:59.204 --> 00:14:01.373
You will see me next week.

